## Why This Is Asked
Tests incident-response planning across Defender for Cloud, Azure AD, Key Vault, and cross-subscription governance.

## Key Concepts
- Automated incident response playbooks
- Key Vault secret rotation
- Managed identities and service principals
- Canary rollouts and rollback strategies
- Cross-subscription isolation and monitoring

## Code Example
```javascript
// Rotate secret using Node.js Azure SDK
const { DefaultAzureCredential } = require('@azure/identity');
const { SecretClient } = require('@azure/keyvault-secrets');
const vault = new SecretClient(`https://${'ProdKV'}.vault.azure.net`, new DefaultAzureCredential());
async function rotate(){ const newVal = require('crypto').randomBytes(32).toString('base64');
  await vault.setSecret('dbPassword', newVal);
}
rotate().catch(console.error);
```

## Why This Is Asked
This question probes practical guardrails for multi-tenant data platforms, focusing on secure upgrades and leakage controls in Azure.

## Key Concepts
- Azure Lighthouse, per-tenant managed identities, least privilege
- Synapse RLS, Data Lake ACLs, per-tenant isolation
- Key Vault rotation, policy gates for secrets in config
- Canary deployments, feature flags, automated rollback
- UEBA monitoring, incident response, runbooks

## Code Example
```javascript
// Example guardrail check: ensure secrets aren't in config
function validateConfig(config) {
  const forbidden = ['AZURE_STORAGE_ACCOUNT_KEY','AZURE_SQL_PASSWORD','SECRET'];
  for (const k of Object.keys(config)) {
    if (forbidden.includes(k.toUpperCase()) || /password|secret|token/i.test(String(config[k]))) {
      throw new Error('Secrets must be stored in Key Vault and not in config');
    }
  }
  return true;
}
```

